        "original_id": "c73a3bd6-6930-580b-8c80-aea4730bff45",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Costus, Boenninghausenia, Boenninghausenia albiflora\n- Taxonomy: Costaceae, Rutaceae, genus, species\n- People: Linnaeus\n- Places: Asia, Africa, the Americas, Bhutan, Nepal, Pakistan, Kashmir, India, Indonesia, Philippines, Myanmar, Thailand, Laos, North Vietnam, China, Japan\n\nFacts:\n- In 1753, Linnaeus described Costus as a genus.\n- Costus is a group of perennial herbaceous plants in the family Costaceae.\n- Costus is widespread through tropical and subtropical regions of Asia, Africa, and the Americas.\n- Boenninghausenia is a monotypic plant genus in the family Rutaceae.\n- Boenninghausenia albiflora is the sole species in the genus Boenninghausenia.\n- Boenninghausenia albiflora occurs in Bhutan, Nepal, Pakistan, Kashmir, India, Indonesia, the Philippines, Myanmar, Thailand, Laos, North Vietnam, China, and Japan.",
